{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PG7YAEnxRpZjoGnHdzELtN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"\"\"CRUD operations on server/data/projects.json. No database - just JSON file read/write.\"\"\"\n     2→import json\n     3→from pathlib import Path\n     4→from typing import Optional\n     5→import shutil\n     6→from server.config import PROJECTS_FILE, DATA_DIR, _LEGACY_DATA_DIR\n     7→from server.models.project import Project\n     8→\n     9→\n    10→def _has_arch_manifest(feature_dir: Path) -> bool:\n    11→    \"\"\"Check if feature has an arch/_arch.json manifest.\"\"\"\n    12→    arch_file = feature_dir / \"arch\" / \"_arch.json\"\n    13→    if not arch_file.exists():\n    14→        return False\n    15→    try:\n    16→        data = json.loads(arch_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    17→        return bool(data and data.get(\"diagrams\"))\n    18→    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n    19→        return False\n    20→\n    21→\n    22→def _count_arch_diagrams(feature_dir: Path) -> int:\n    23→    \"\"\"Count .mmd and .drawio files in the arch/ directory.\"\"\"\n    24→    arch_dir = feature_dir / \"arch\"\n    25→    if not arch_dir.exists():\n    26→        return 0\n    27→    count = len(list(arch_dir.glob(\"*.mmd\")))\n    28→    count += len(list(arch_dir.glob(\"*.drawio\")))\n    29→    return count\n    30→\n    31→\n    32→class ProjectService:\n    33→    \"\"\"Manages the project registry stored in projects.json.\"\"\"\n    34→\n    35→    _migrated = False\n    36→\n    37→    @staticmethod\n    38→    def _migrate_legacy_data():\n    39→        \"\"\"One-time migration from plugin-internal data dir to ~/.vista/data/.\"\"\"\n    40→        if ProjectService._migrated:\n    41→            return\n    42→        ProjectService._migrated = True\n    43→\n    44→        legacy_projects = _LEGACY_DATA_DIR / \"projects.json\"\n    45→        if legacy_projects.exists() and not PROJECTS_FILE.exists():\n    46→            DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    47→            shutil.copy2(legacy_projects, PROJECTS_FILE)\n    48→\n    49→        # Also migrate sessions/ if present\n    50→        legacy_sessions = _LEGACY_DATA_DIR / \"sessions\"\n    51→        new_sessions = DATA_DIR / \"sessions\"\n    52→        if legacy_sessions.is_dir() and not new_sessions.exists():\n    53→            DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    54→            shutil.copytree(legacy_sessions, new_sessions)\n    55→\n    56→    @staticmethod\n    57→    def _ensure_file():\n    58→        \"\"\"Create data directory and projects.json if they don't exist.\"\"\"\n    59→        ProjectService._migrate_legacy_data()\n    60→        DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    61→        if not PROJECTS_FILE.exists():\n    62→            PROJECTS_FILE.write_text(\"[]\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    63→\n    64→    @staticmethod\n    65→    def _load() -> list[dict]:\n    66→        ProjectService._ensure_file()\n    67→        return json.loads(PROJECTS_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    68→\n    69→    @staticmethod\n    70→    def _save(projects: list[dict]):\n    71→        ProjectService._ensure_file()\n    72→        PROJECTS_FILE.write_text(json.dumps(projects, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    73→\n    74→    @staticmethod\n    75→    def get_all() -> list[Project]:\n    76→        \"\"\"Return all registered projects.\"\"\"\n    77→        return [Project.from_dict(p) for p in ProjectService._load()]\n    78→\n    79→    @staticmethod\n    80→    def get_by_id(project_id: str) -> Optional[Project]:\n    81→        \"\"\"Get a single project by ID.\"\"\"\n    82→        for p in ProjectService._load():\n    83→            if p[\"id\"] == project_id:\n    84→                return Project.from_dict(p)\n    85→        return None\n    86→\n    87→    @staticmethod\n    88→    def register(path: str) -> Project:\n    89→        \"\"\"Register a new project. Validates path exists.\"\"\"\n    90→        abs_path = Path(path).resolve()\n    91→        if not abs_path.is_dir():\n    92→            raise ValueError(f\"Path does not exist or is not a directory: {path}\")\n    93→\n    94→        projects = ProjectService._load()\n    95→\n    96→        # Check for duplicate path\n    97→        for p in projects:\n    98→            if Path(p[\"path\"]).resolve() == abs_path:\n    99→                raise ValueError(f\"Project already registered: {abs_path}\")\n   100→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWjZvNU1MyBFPkJ6FSAJK4","session_id":"fe920b97-a686-4daa-9f39-67e009025eb9","uuid":"d80478b1-2902-4a77-9722-4df92877d9e7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWjZvNU1MyBFPkJ6FSAJK4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the Vista server codebase. Let me create a detailed analysis document.\n\n## Analysis: Vista Server Codebase Structure\n\n### Overview\nThe Vista server is a FastAPI-based web dashboard for managing AI-powered feature planning and implementation loops. It provides both a web UI and MCP (Model Context Protocol) tools for spawning Claude/OpenCode agents in tmux sessions, managing project loops, and facilitating architecture diagram review via persistent chat sessions. The server runs as a daemon thread within the MCP server process (C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\mcp_server.py:92-101).\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n#### Server Core (`vista/server/`)\n- **`app.py`**: FastAPI application entry point with lifespan management\n- **`config.py`**: Configuration loader with settings file management at `~/.vista/settings.json`\n- **`mcp_server.py`**: MCP server wrapping the FastAPI dashboard as daemon thread\n\n#### Models (`vista/server/models/`)\n- **`chat_session.py`**: ChatSession and ChatMessage dataclasses for persistent chat\n- **`project.py`**: Project model for registered repositories\n- **`loop_state.py`**: LoopInstance tracking for running feature loops\n- **`sandbox.py`**: Docker sandbox configuration models\n\n#### Services (`vista/server/services/`)\nCore business logic organized by domain:\n\n- **`chat_service.py`**: AI provider invocation (blocking + streaming)\n- **`chat_session_service.py`**: Session persistence to JSON files at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/`\n- **`diagram_watcher.py`**: File polling watcher for architecture diagram changes\n- **`keepalive_manager.py`**: Persistent Claude agent lifecycle via tmux + inbox messaging\n- **`loop_service.py`**: Feature loop execution (plan/build modes)\n- **`output_parser.py`**: Parses loop script stdout for structured events\n- **`project_service.py`**: Project registry CRUD at `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- **`provider_service.py`**: Multi-provider abstraction (Claude, OpenCode)\n- **`ralph_service.py`**: Ralph job lifecycle (native subprocess + Docker sandbox)\n- **`progress_service.py`**: Feature directory scanning and arch manifest reading\n- **`summarizer_service.py`**: AI-powered progress summarization\n\nSandbox subsystem (`vista/server/services/sandbox/`):\n- **`container_manager.py`**: Docker container lifecycle\n- **`credential_mounter.py`**: Mount credentials into containers\n- **`bash_loop_generator.py`**: Generate bash loop scripts for sandbox execution\n- **`docker_client.py`**: Docker API wrapper\n\n#### Routes (`vista/server/routes/`)\nFastAPI router modules:\n\n- **`architecture.py`**: Diagram viewing endpoints\n- **`chat.py`**: Legacy one-shot chat endpoint (POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/chat`)\n- **`chat_sessions.py`**: Session-based chat with SSE streaming\n- **`loops.py`**: Feature loop control API\n- **`plans.py`**: Plan mode endpoints\n- **`projects.py`**: Project registration and listing\n- **`providers.py`**: Provider discovery and model enumeration\n- **`ralph.py`**: Ralph job status and progress endpoints\n- **`ralph_settings.py`**: Ralph configuration management\n- **`sandbox.py`**: Sandbox configuration and control\n- **`shutdown.py`**: Server shutdown endpoint\n- **`stream.py`**: SSE streaming for loop activity\n\n#### Tests (`vista/tests/`)\n- Unit tests for services and parsers\n- Integration tests in `tests/integration/`\n- `conftest.py` with pytest fixtures\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n#### 1. Application Lifecycle (`app.py:22-32`)\n\n```python\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    config.ensure_full_path()\n    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    yield\n    await loop_service.stop_all()\n    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n    keepalive_manager.stop_all()\n```\n\n- Ensures data directories exist at startup\n- Cleans up running loops and persistent agents on shutdown\n- DATA_DIR resolves to `~/.vista/data/` (config.py:13)\n\n#### 2. Chat Service Architecture\n\n##### Provider Abstraction (`provider_service.py:93-172`)\n\n**Base Provider class** defines the interface:\n- `get_models()`: List available models\n- `get_invocation(shell)`: Return shell snippet for loop scripts\n- `get_chat_cmd(model, streaming, permissions)`: Build CLI command list\n- `get_persistent_cmd(model, permissions)`: Interactive mode command\n- `parse_stream_event(line)`: Parse streaming JSON output\n\n**ClaudeProvider** (`provider_service.py:174-247`):\n- Models: `[\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]` (line 179)\n- Streaming via `--output-format=stream-json` flag (line 214)\n- Parses JSON events: `{\"type\": \"assistant\", \"text\": \"...\"}` (line 235-238)\n- Persistent mode uses interactive flag (no `-p`) at line 224\n\n**OpenCodeProvider** (`provider_service.py:249-298`):\n- Discovers models via `opencode models` CLI at line 259\n- Non-streaming: prompt passed as positional arg (line 291)\n- No persistent mode support (returns None)\n\n##### Chat Service Implementation (`chat_service.py:37-305`)\n\n**Singleton service** with cancellation support via `_active_proc` tracking (line 41).\n\n**Blocking invocation** (`invoke_provider`, line 104-172):\n- Runs via `asyncio.to_thread()` to avoid blocking event loop\n- Timeout default: 90 seconds (line 109)\n- Handles stdin piping for Claude, positional args for OpenCode (line 139-143)\n- Windows: Uses `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` flag and `taskkill /T /F` for tree kill (line 24-34)\n\n**Streaming invocation** (`invoke_provider_streaming`, line 174-301):\n- AsyncGenerator yielding event dicts: `{\"type\": \"token\"|\"done\"|\"error\", ...}`\n- Delegates to provider's `parse_stream_event()` for format parsing (line 261)\n- Non-streaming fallback: yields all output at once (line 278-292)\n- Cancellation: Kills subprocess on `asyncio.CancelledError` (line 294-295)\n\n**Prompt builder** (`build_prompt`, line 54-102):\n- Assembles context, history, and user message\n- For arch chat: includes file access instructions with project root and arch dir boundaries (line 65-74)\n- Format: context → history → user message → \"ASSISTANT:\" prompt (line 98-100)\n\n#### 3. Chat Session Management\n\n##### Session Model (`models/chat_session.py:29-107`)\n\n**ChatSession dataclass**:\n- Fields: id, project_id, feature_name, provider, model, messages, created_at, updated_at, team_name\n- `team_name` links to keepalive_manager's persistent agent (line 42)\n- `to_summary_dict()` excludes message bodies for lightweight listing (line 65-78)\n- Auto-generates 8-char hex ID via `uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]` (line 98)\n\n**ChatMessage dataclass** (line 9-27):\n- Fields: role (\"user\"|\"assistant\"), content, timestamp\n- Auto-populates ISO timestamp on creation (line 17-19)\n\n##### Session Persistence (`services/chat_session_service.py:1-124`)\n\n**File-based storage** at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` (line 14, 26).\n\n**CRUD operations**:\n- `create()`: Generates new session with unique ID (line 28-46)\n- `list_sessions()`: Returns summary dicts sorted by mtime, optionally filtered by feature (line 48-65)\n- `get()`: Loads full session from JSON file (line 68-72)\n- `delete()`: Unlinks file (line 75-80)\n- `add_message()`: Appends message, updates timestamp, auto-names from first user message (line 83-96)\n- `update_name()`: Renames session (line 99-106)\n\n**Auto-naming**: First user message generates session name via `ChatSession.auto_name()` (line 93-94, models/chat_session.py:101-106).\n\n##### Session Routes (`routes/chat_sessions.py:1-420`)\n\n**Session CRUD endpoints**:\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions`: List sessions (line 85-90)\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions`: Create session (line 93-133)\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Get session details (line 136-141)\n- `DELETE /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Delete session and stop agent (line 144-152)\n- `PATCH /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Rename session (line 155-160)\n\n**Message sending** (`POST /messages`, line 167-257):\n- Saves user message immediately (line 192)\n- Supports mode toggle: \"oneshot\" or \"persistent\" (line 74, 198)\n- **Oneshot mode**: Full history replayed each time, spawns background streaming task (line 243-255)\n- **Persistent mode**: Sends message to keepalive agent via inbox, polls for response (line 200-241)\n- Provider/model can be overridden per message (line 182-189)\n\n**SSE streaming** (`GET /stream`, line 369-419):\n- Merges two asyncio.Queue sources: chat events + diagram watcher events (line 384-395)\n- Forwards both to client via merged queue (line 391)\n- 30-second timeout with ping keepalive (line 401-407)\n- On disconnect: schedules 10-second grace period before killing persistent agent (line 417)\n- On reconnect: cancels pending disconnect cleanup (line 381)\n\n**Internal pub-sub** (line 22-54):\n- `_session_subscribers` dict maps session_id → list of Queue objects\n- `_broadcast()` pushes events to all subscribers for a session (line 43-54)\n- Background tasks call `_broadcast()` to push tokens/errors to SSE clients (line 280-305, 314-336)\n\n#### 4. Keep-Alive Manager (`services/keepalive_manager.py:1-470`)\n\n**Singleton persistent agent** via tmux + file-based messaging (line 73-74).\n\n**Architecture**:\n- At most one tmux pane active at a time (line 77, 98)\n- Uses `claude-teams` library for inbox messaging (imported at line 21-27)\n- Team directory: `~/.claude/teams/vista-chat-{session_id}` (line 31, 101)\n\n**Lifecycle methods**:\n\n**`start()`** (line 85-139):\n- Kills existing agent if any (line 98-99)\n- Creates team via `teams.create_team()` (line 111)\n- Spawns Claude agent in tmux pane (line 117-126)\n- Stores `_LiveSession` dataclass with session_id, team_name, pane_id (line 133-138)\n\n**`send_message()`** (line 141-160):\n- Validates session matches current agent (line 145-146)\n- Sends plain message via `messaging.send_plain_message()` to \"architect\" agent (line 154-160)\n\n**`poll_response()`** (line 162-199):\n- AsyncGenerator that polls agent inbox every 0.5s (line 174)\n- Reads unread messages via `messaging.read_inbox()` (line 177-182)\n- Yields first message from \"architect\" as token + done event (line 184-189)\n- Timeout after 120s (line 163, 199)\n- Bails early if pane dies (line 195-197)\n\n**`resume()`** (line 207-231):\n- Attempts to reconnect to existing team/pane from previous session\n- Validates pane is still alive via `_is_pane_alive()` (line 219)\n- Restores internal state if successful (line 220-226)\n\n**`stop()`** (line 233-246):\n- Cancels disconnect cleanup task (line 238)\n- Kills tmux pane via `_tmux_kill_pane()` (line 244)\n- Force-deletes team directories (line 245)\n\n**Disconnect grace period** (line 272-292):\n- `schedule_disconnect_cleanup()`: Starts 10-second timer on SSE disconnect (line 272-286)\n- `cancel_disconnect_cleanup()`: Cancels timer on SSE reconnect (line 288-292)\n- Prevents killing agent if user's browser momentarily loses connection\n\n**Tmux spawning** (`_spawn_agent`, line 335-422):\n- Bypasses `spawn_teammate()` due to MSYS2 tmux bug with `#{pane_id}` format strings (line 11, 347)\n- Snapshot pane IDs before spawn, diff after to find new pane (line 388-404)\n- Uses `%N` format (stable unique ID) instead of `session:window.pane` (line 350)\n- Updates team config with actual pane ID (line 407-412)\n\n**Tmux detection** (line 34-56):\n- Searches for tmux in standard MSYS2 paths on Windows (line 35-37)\n- Adds to PATH if found (line 42-51)\n\n#### 5. Diagram Watcher (`services/diagram_watcher.py:1-161`)\n\n**Polling-based file watcher** for `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 16).\n\n**Architecture**:\n- Polls every 2 seconds (line 15)\n- Tracks mtime per file in `_file_states` dict (line 22)\n- Single background `_poll_loop` task serves all subscriptions (line 27, 48-49)\n\n**Subscription model** (line 32-65):\n- `subscribe()` returns an asyncio.Queue for the caller (line 32-51)\n- Multiple subscribers per `{project_id}:{feature_name}` key (line 29, 38-45)\n- `unsubscribe()` removes queue and cleans up when no subscribers remain (line 53-65)\n\n**Events** (line 91-114):\n- `diagram_added`: New file detected (line 95-100)\n- `diagram_changed`: mtime changed (line 101-106)\n- `diagram_removed`: File no longer exists (line 109-114)\n- Each event includes file content (line 96, 102) read via `_read_file()` (line 139-144)\n\n**Broadcasting** (line 119-137):\n- `_broadcast()` pushes event dict to all subscriber queues (line 126-137)\n- Dead queues (QueueFull) are automatically removed (line 129-137)\n\n#### 6. Configuration (`config.py:1-300`)\n\n**Directory structure** (line 8-17):\n- `PLUGIN_ROOT`: Plugin install directory (`vista/`)\n- `PORTABLE_DIR`: `vista/portable/` (loop script templates)\n- `DATA_DIR`: `~/.vista/data/` (persistent data, migrated from plugin dir in v1.3.12)\n- `PROJECTS_FILE`: `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- `SETTINGS_FILE`: `~/.vista/settings.json` (configurable via `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` env var)\n\n**Settings structure**:\n- `server`: auto_start, auto_open_browser, host, port (line 38-43)\n- `ralph`: defaults, summarizer, providers, sandbox (line 45-70)\n- `tools.teams`: claude_binary, opencode_url, opencode_auto_start (line 72-80)\n\n**Loading and merging** (line 91-138):\n- `load_settings()`: Reads JSON file, returns `{}` on failure (line 91-99)\n- `_merge_dicts()`: Recursive dict merge (line 123-130)\n- `get_ralph_settings()`: Merges defaults with user overrides (line 133-138)\n- `get_server_settings()`: Env vars override JSON (line 229-252)\n\n**Legacy migration** (line 102-121):\n- One-time migration from `vista/settings.json` to `~/.vista/settings.json` (line 102-120)\n- Non-fatal if migration fails (line 118-120)\n\n**Windows PATH fix** (`ensure_full_path`, line 255-293):\n- Merges system+user PATH from registry on Windows (line 267-288)\n- Fixes stripped PATH in git-bash/IDE contexts (line 257-261)\n- Safe to call multiple times (line 263)\n\n#### 7. Ralph Service (`services/ralph_service.py:1-100+`)\n\n**Job lifecycle manager** for native subprocess and Docker sandbox execution.\n\n**Job creation** (line 40-59):\n- Routes to `_create_native_job()` or `_create_sandboxed_job()` based on `sandbox` flag (line 51-58)\n- Generates UUID job_id (line 72)\n- Job directory: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` (line 73)\n\n**Native job flow** (`_create_native_job`, line 61-100+):\n- Clears runtime artifacts (`output.log`, `loop.ps1`, etc.) at line 76\n- **Plan mode feature dir resolution**: If mode==\"plan\" and feature dir exists, use it as working dir instead of job dir (line 82-83)\n  - This ensures multiple plan loops overwrite the same `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (line 81)\n- Writes `task.md` to feature dir (line 85-86)\n- Generates prompt file from template (line 88-98)\n- Generates loop script from `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` (imported from `portable/ralph.py` at line 16)\n\n**Provider integration** (line 19):\n- Imports `Provider` class from `provider_service.py`\n- Provider's `get_invocation()` method generates shell snippet for loop script\n\n**Output parsing** (line 18):\n- Imports `parse_plaintext_activity` and `parse_stream_json_activity`\n- Parser dispatch logic in ralph routes (routes/ralph.py:88-91)\n\n**Sandbox support** (line 21-29):\n- Lazy-imports Docker-related modules only when `sandbox=True`\n- Modules: `ContainerManager`, `CredentialMounter`, `BashLoopGenerator`\n- Avoids Docker SDK dependency for native jobs\n\n#### 8. Application Entry Point (`app.py:34-334`)\n\n**FastAPI app** created at line 34 with lifespan context manager.\n\n**Router registration** (line 44-70):\n- Imports all route modules (line 44-57)\n- Includes routers via `app.include_router()` (line 59-70)\n\n**Dashboard pages**:\n- `GET /`: Project list dashboard (line 177-203)\n- `GET /project/{project_id}`: Project detail with loop controls (line 206-233)\n- `GET /ralph/jobs`: Ralph jobs list (line 236-254)\n- `GET /ralph/jobs/{job_id}`: Job detail with progress/artifacts (line 257-327)\n- `GET /ralph/settings`: Settings configuration page (line 330-333)\n\n**API endpoints**:\n- `GET /api/health`: Health check with running loop count (line 73-85)\n- `GET /api/loops/running`: Active loops summary for global status bar (line 88-174)\n  - Merges project loops and ralph jobs (line 123-171)\n  - Refreshes ralph job PIDs to avoid stale \"running\" status (line 130-133)\n\n**Loop activity aggregation** (line 88-174):\n- Collects from two sources: `loop_service.get_all_states()` and `ralph_service.list_jobs()`\n- Includes recent actions (last 3) for each loop (line 103, 136-145)\n- Calculates progress percentage from iteration/max_iterations (line 98-100, 147-151)\n- Returns unified list sorted by start_time (line 173-174)\n\n#### 9. MCP Server (`mcp_server.py:1-200`)\n\n**Process model**: MCP server (stdio) wraps FastAPI dashboard as daemon thread (line 1-9).\n\n**Dashboard thread** (`_run_uvicorn_in_thread`, line 92-101):\n- Imports `server.app` at runtime (line 95)\n- Creates `uvicorn.Server` with `log_level=\"warning\"` (line 97)\n- Starts in daemon thread (line 99-100)\n\n**Port allocation** (`_find_free_port`, line 80-89):\n- Incrementally searches for available port starting from preferred (line 82-88)\n\n**OpenCode server launcher** (`_start_opencode_serve`, line 116-144):\n- Spawns `opencode serve --port {port}` subprocess (line 122-127)\n- Polls `/agent` endpoint for up to 10s to confirm readiness (line 130-143)\n\n**Spawn tool description builder** (line 150-200):\n- Dynamically generates tool description based on discovered backends/models\n- Lists available Claude models (line 176) and OpenCode models (line 178-181)\n- Includes OpenCode agent types if server is running (line 184-191)\n\n### Data Flow\n\n#### Chat Session Flow (Persistent Mode)\n\n1. **Session creation** (`POST /api/projects/{pid}/chat/sessions`, chat_sessions.py:93)\n   - Creates ChatSession model (line 99-105)\n   - If mode==\"persistent\": spawns Claude agent via `keepalive_manager.start()` (line 108-128)\n   - Returns session dict with team_name (line 133)\n\n2. **Message send** (`POST /sessions/{sid}/messages`, line 167)\n   - Saves user message (line 192)\n   - Checks if agent is alive via `keepalive_manager.is_alive()` (line 202)\n   - If dead but team_name exists: attempts `keepalive_manager.resume()` (line 205-206)\n   - If still dead: cold starts agent with full history (line 209-228)\n   - If alive: sends just the new message via `keepalive_manager.send_message()` (line 237)\n   - Spawns background task `_stream_response_keepalive()` (line 239-241)\n\n3. **Response streaming** (`_stream_response_keepalive`, line 308)\n   - Polls agent inbox via `keepalive_manager.poll_response()` (line 314)\n   - Broadcasts token events to SSE subscribers (line 315-319)\n   - Saves assistant message when done (line 322)\n   - Broadcasts message_done event (line 323-326)\n\n4. **SSE client connection** (`GET /sessions/{sid}/stream`, line 369)\n   - Subscribes to chat queue (line 384)\n   - Subscribes to diagram watcher queue (line 388)\n   - Merges both queues via forwarder tasks (line 394-395)\n   - Yields events to client (line 401-407)\n   - On disconnect: schedules 10s grace period to kill agent (line 417)\n\n#### Ralph Job Flow (Native)\n\n1. **Job creation** (ralph_service.py:40-59)\n   - Calls `_create_native_job()` (line 56-59)\n   - Generates job dir: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` (line 73)\n   - Writes task.md, prompt, and loop script (line 85-98)\n\n2. **Job execution** (not shown in read sections)\n   - Spawns subprocess running loop script\n   - Script streams output to `output.log`\n   - Script writes progress summaries to `progress.txt`\n\n3. **Status monitoring** (routes/ralph.py:56-65)\n   - `get_job_status()` reads `job.json` + checks PID liveness\n   - Returns status dict with current iteration, progress tail\n\n4. **Progress display** (routes/ralph.py:68-92)\n   - Dashboard always reads `output.log` (line 74)\n   - Dispatches to parser based on provider: `parse_stream_json_activity` for Claude, `parse_plaintext_activity` for others (line 88-91)\n   - Returns last N parsed activity lines (line 92)\n\n### Key Patterns\n\n#### Publisher-Subscriber Pattern\n\n**LoopService** (not fully shown but referenced in app.py:29, 77-79):\n- Broadcasts loop state changes to SSE clients\n- Multiple routes subscribe to loop activity\n\n**DiagramWatcher** (diagram_watcher.py:12-161):\n- Polls file system, broadcasts changes to subscribers\n- Each SSE client gets a dedicated queue (line 44)\n\n**ChatSessionRoutes** (chat_sessions.py:22-54):\n- Internal pub-sub for chat events\n- Background tasks broadcast to all SSE connections for a session\n\n#### Service Layer Pattern\n\nAll business logic encapsulated in `server/services/`:\n- Routes are thin wrappers calling service methods\n- Services manage state and persistence\n- Clear separation: routes handle HTTP, services handle domain logic\n\n#### Provider Strategy Pattern\n\n**Provider base class** (provider_service.py:93-172):\n- Abstract interface for CLI agent providers\n- Implementations: ClaudeProvider, OpenCodeProvider\n- Allows adding new providers without changing core logic\n\n#### File-Based Persistence\n\n**No database**: All data stored as JSON files:\n- Projects: `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- Sessions: `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`\n- Settings: `~/.vista/settings.json`\n- Job metadata: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/job.json`\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Settings file**: `~/.vista/settings.json` (config.py:36)\n\n**Environment variable overrides** (config.py:235-250):\n- `RALPH_SERVER_HOST` → server.host\n- `RALPH_SERVER_PORT` → server.port\n- `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_START` → server.auto_start (bool)\n- `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_OPEN` → server.auto_open_browser (bool)\n- `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` → custom settings path (line 28-32)\n\n**Ralph defaults** (config.py:46-56):\n- Provider: \"claude\"\n- Model: \"sonnet\"\n- Iterations: 3\n- Summarizer: claude/haiku\n\n**Sandbox defaults** (config.py:58-70):\n- Enabled: false\n- Image: \"vista-ralph:latest\"\n- Network: enabled\n- TTL: 7200 seconds\n- Credential mounts: claude_auth, git_ssh, git_config, gh_cli, opencode (all enabled)\n\n### Error Handling\n\n**Chat service** (chat_service.py):\n- Timeout: Returns error tuple `(False, \"Request timed out\")` (line 161)\n- CLI error: Returns `(False, f\"CLI error (code {rc}): {stderr}\")` (line 167-170)\n- Cancellation: Returns `(False, \"Request was cancelled\")` (line 169)\n\n**Streaming** (chat_service.py:174-301):\n- Yields `{\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": \"...\"}` on failure (line 188, 274, 297)\n- Catches `asyncio.CancelledError` to call `cancel()` (line 294-295)\n\n**Keep-alive manager** (keepalive_manager.py):\n- Poll timeout: Yields error event after 120s (line 199)\n- Pane death: Yields error event immediately (line 196)\n\n**Ralph service** (ralph_service.py):\n- Raises `ValueError` if prompt template not found (line 95)\n\n### Dependencies\n\n**Key external libraries** (inferred from imports):\n- `fastapi`: Web framework\n- `uvicorn`: ASGI server\n- `sse_starlette`: Server-sent events support (chat_sessions.py:11)\n- `pydantic`: Request/response validation\n- `claude_teams`: Claude agent spawning and messaging (keepalive_manager.py:21-27)\n- `fastmcp`: MCP protocol implementation (mcp_server.py:35-38)\n\n**Docker SDK** (optional, lazy-imported):\n- `docker`: Container management (ralph_service.py:27-29)\n- Only imported when sandbox mode is enabled\n\n### Plugin Manifest\n\n**File**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\.claude-plugin\\plugin.json`\n\n**Current version**: 1.3.15 (line 3)\n\n**Metadata**:\n- Name: \"vista\"\n- Description: \"Visual feature planning with review gate between specs and implementation\"\n- Author: Grove\n- Keywords: planning, visualization, review, feature, jtbd\n\n### Test Structure (`vista/tests/`)\n\n**Unit tests**:\n- `test_output_parser.py`: Parser logic\n- `test_progress_service.py`: Feature scanning\n- `test_project_service.py`: Project CRUD\n- `test_loop_service.py`: Loop lifecycle\n- `test_ralph_service.py`: Ralph job management\n- `test_summarizer_service.py`: AI summarization\n- Sandbox-related: `test_docker_client.py`, `test_container_manager.py`, `test_credential_mounter.py`, `test_bash_loop_generator.py`\n\n**Integration tests** (`tests/integration/`):\n- `test_ralph_lifecycle.py`: End-to-end ralph job flow\n- `test_mcp_tools.py`: MCP tool invocation\n- `test_docker_sandbox.py`: Sandbox execution\n\n**Test fixtures** (`conftest.py`):\n- Provides shared fixtures for projects, sessions, temp directories\n\n### Key Files Referenced\n\nAll absolute paths:\n\n- **Server entry**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\app.py`\n- **MCP wrapper**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\mcp_server.py`\n- **Config**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\config.py`\n- **Chat models**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py`\n- **Chat service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_service.py`\n- **Session service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py`\n- **Keep-alive manager**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\keepalive_manager.py`\n- **Diagram watcher**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\diagram_watcher.py`\n- **Provider service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\provider_service.py`\n- **Ralph service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py`\n- **Output parser**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\output_parser.py`\n- **Session routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat_sessions.py`\n- **Chat routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat.py`\n- **Ralph routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py`\n- **Architecture routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\architecture.py`\n- **Plugin manifest**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\.claude-plugin\\plugin.json`\n\nThis analysis documents the Vista server codebase as it exists in version 1.3.15, focusing on the architecture and implementation of the chat session system, persistent agents, diagram watching, and multi-provider support."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a3f9013 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 63771\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 205014</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe920b97-a686-4daa-9f39-67e009025eb9","uuid":"c8d2eac2-67e7-4093-82c2-3ae7d191926c","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the vista server codebase to understand the current structure. I need to understand:\n\n1. The directory structure under `vista/server/` - all files\n2. The directory structure under `vista/tests/` - all files\n3. The current `server/app.py` - full contents\n4. The current `server/config.py` - full contents\n5. The current `server/services/` directory - all files and their key classes\n6. The current `server/routes/` directory - all files\n7. The current `server/models/chat_session.py` if it exists\n8. The current `mcp_server.py` - just the imports and the `_start_opencode_serve` function\n9. The current `server/services/diagram_watcher.py` - full contents\n10. The current `server/services/chat_service.py` - full contents\n11. The current `server/routes/chat_sessions.py` - full contents  \n12. The current `server/services/keepalive_manager.py` if it exists\n13. The current `server/routes/chat.py` if it exists\n14. Any existing requirements.txt or pyproject.toml for dependencies\n15. The plugin.json manifest for current version\n\nFocus on reading the actual file contents, especially for the files that will be modified or serve as templates for new files.","agentId":"a3f9013","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the Vista server codebase. Let me create a detailed analysis document.\n\n## Analysis: Vista Server Codebase Structure\n\n### Overview\nThe Vista server is a FastAPI-based web dashboard for managing AI-powered feature planning and implementation loops. It provides both a web UI and MCP (Model Context Protocol) tools for spawning Claude/OpenCode agents in tmux sessions, managing project loops, and facilitating architecture diagram review via persistent chat sessions. The server runs as a daemon thread within the MCP server process (C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\mcp_server.py:92-101).\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n#### Server Core (`vista/server/`)\n- **`app.py`**: FastAPI application entry point with lifespan management\n- **`config.py`**: Configuration loader with settings file management at `~/.vista/settings.json`\n- **`mcp_server.py`**: MCP server wrapping the FastAPI dashboard as daemon thread\n\n#### Models (`vista/server/models/`)\n- **`chat_session.py`**: ChatSession and ChatMessage dataclasses for persistent chat\n- **`project.py`**: Project model for registered repositories\n- **`loop_state.py`**: LoopInstance tracking for running feature loops\n- **`sandbox.py`**: Docker sandbox configuration models\n\n#### Services (`vista/server/services/`)\nCore business logic organized by domain:\n\n- **`chat_service.py`**: AI provider invocation (blocking + streaming)\n- **`chat_session_service.py`**: Session persistence to JSON files at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/`\n- **`diagram_watcher.py`**: File polling watcher for architecture diagram changes\n- **`keepalive_manager.py`**: Persistent Claude agent lifecycle via tmux + inbox messaging\n- **`loop_service.py`**: Feature loop execution (plan/build modes)\n- **`output_parser.py`**: Parses loop script stdout for structured events\n- **`project_service.py`**: Project registry CRUD at `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- **`provider_service.py`**: Multi-provider abstraction (Claude, OpenCode)\n- **`ralph_service.py`**: Ralph job lifecycle (native subprocess + Docker sandbox)\n- **`progress_service.py`**: Feature directory scanning and arch manifest reading\n- **`summarizer_service.py`**: AI-powered progress summarization\n\nSandbox subsystem (`vista/server/services/sandbox/`):\n- **`container_manager.py`**: Docker container lifecycle\n- **`credential_mounter.py`**: Mount credentials into containers\n- **`bash_loop_generator.py`**: Generate bash loop scripts for sandbox execution\n- **`docker_client.py`**: Docker API wrapper\n\n#### Routes (`vista/server/routes/`)\nFastAPI router modules:\n\n- **`architecture.py`**: Diagram viewing endpoints\n- **`chat.py`**: Legacy one-shot chat endpoint (POST `/api/projects/{project_id}/chat`)\n- **`chat_sessions.py`**: Session-based chat with SSE streaming\n- **`loops.py`**: Feature loop control API\n- **`plans.py`**: Plan mode endpoints\n- **`projects.py`**: Project registration and listing\n- **`providers.py`**: Provider discovery and model enumeration\n- **`ralph.py`**: Ralph job status and progress endpoints\n- **`ralph_settings.py`**: Ralph configuration management\n- **`sandbox.py`**: Sandbox configuration and control\n- **`shutdown.py`**: Server shutdown endpoint\n- **`stream.py`**: SSE streaming for loop activity\n\n#### Tests (`vista/tests/`)\n- Unit tests for services and parsers\n- Integration tests in `tests/integration/`\n- `conftest.py` with pytest fixtures\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n#### 1. Application Lifecycle (`app.py:22-32`)\n\n```python\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    config.ensure_full_path()\n    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    yield\n    await loop_service.stop_all()\n    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n    keepalive_manager.stop_all()\n```\n\n- Ensures data directories exist at startup\n- Cleans up running loops and persistent agents on shutdown\n- DATA_DIR resolves to `~/.vista/data/` (config.py:13)\n\n#### 2. Chat Service Architecture\n\n##### Provider Abstraction (`provider_service.py:93-172`)\n\n**Base Provider class** defines the interface:\n- `get_models()`: List available models\n- `get_invocation(shell)`: Return shell snippet for loop scripts\n- `get_chat_cmd(model, streaming, permissions)`: Build CLI command list\n- `get_persistent_cmd(model, permissions)`: Interactive mode command\n- `parse_stream_event(line)`: Parse streaming JSON output\n\n**ClaudeProvider** (`provider_service.py:174-247`):\n- Models: `[\"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\"]` (line 179)\n- Streaming via `--output-format=stream-json` flag (line 214)\n- Parses JSON events: `{\"type\": \"assistant\", \"text\": \"...\"}` (line 235-238)\n- Persistent mode uses interactive flag (no `-p`) at line 224\n\n**OpenCodeProvider** (`provider_service.py:249-298`):\n- Discovers models via `opencode models` CLI at line 259\n- Non-streaming: prompt passed as positional arg (line 291)\n- No persistent mode support (returns None)\n\n##### Chat Service Implementation (`chat_service.py:37-305`)\n\n**Singleton service** with cancellation support via `_active_proc` tracking (line 41).\n\n**Blocking invocation** (`invoke_provider`, line 104-172):\n- Runs via `asyncio.to_thread()` to avoid blocking event loop\n- Timeout default: 90 seconds (line 109)\n- Handles stdin piping for Claude, positional args for OpenCode (line 139-143)\n- Windows: Uses `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` flag and `taskkill /T /F` for tree kill (line 24-34)\n\n**Streaming invocation** (`invoke_provider_streaming`, line 174-301):\n- AsyncGenerator yielding event dicts: `{\"type\": \"token\"|\"done\"|\"error\", ...}`\n- Delegates to provider's `parse_stream_event()` for format parsing (line 261)\n- Non-streaming fallback: yields all output at once (line 278-292)\n- Cancellation: Kills subprocess on `asyncio.CancelledError` (line 294-295)\n\n**Prompt builder** (`build_prompt`, line 54-102):\n- Assembles context, history, and user message\n- For arch chat: includes file access instructions with project root and arch dir boundaries (line 65-74)\n- Format: context → history → user message → \"ASSISTANT:\" prompt (line 98-100)\n\n#### 3. Chat Session Management\n\n##### Session Model (`models/chat_session.py:29-107`)\n\n**ChatSession dataclass**:\n- Fields: id, project_id, feature_name, provider, model, messages, created_at, updated_at, team_name\n- `team_name` links to keepalive_manager's persistent agent (line 42)\n- `to_summary_dict()` excludes message bodies for lightweight listing (line 65-78)\n- Auto-generates 8-char hex ID via `uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]` (line 98)\n\n**ChatMessage dataclass** (line 9-27):\n- Fields: role (\"user\"|\"assistant\"), content, timestamp\n- Auto-populates ISO timestamp on creation (line 17-19)\n\n##### Session Persistence (`services/chat_session_service.py:1-124`)\n\n**File-based storage** at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` (line 14, 26).\n\n**CRUD operations**:\n- `create()`: Generates new session with unique ID (line 28-46)\n- `list_sessions()`: Returns summary dicts sorted by mtime, optionally filtered by feature (line 48-65)\n- `get()`: Loads full session from JSON file (line 68-72)\n- `delete()`: Unlinks file (line 75-80)\n- `add_message()`: Appends message, updates timestamp, auto-names from first user message (line 83-96)\n- `update_name()`: Renames session (line 99-106)\n\n**Auto-naming**: First user message generates session name via `ChatSession.auto_name()` (line 93-94, models/chat_session.py:101-106).\n\n##### Session Routes (`routes/chat_sessions.py:1-420`)\n\n**Session CRUD endpoints**:\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions`: List sessions (line 85-90)\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions`: Create session (line 93-133)\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Get session details (line 136-141)\n- `DELETE /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Delete session and stop agent (line 144-152)\n- `PATCH /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}`: Rename session (line 155-160)\n\n**Message sending** (`POST /messages`, line 167-257):\n- Saves user message immediately (line 192)\n- Supports mode toggle: \"oneshot\" or \"persistent\" (line 74, 198)\n- **Oneshot mode**: Full history replayed each time, spawns background streaming task (line 243-255)\n- **Persistent mode**: Sends message to keepalive agent via inbox, polls for response (line 200-241)\n- Provider/model can be overridden per message (line 182-189)\n\n**SSE streaming** (`GET /stream`, line 369-419):\n- Merges two asyncio.Queue sources: chat events + diagram watcher events (line 384-395)\n- Forwards both to client via merged queue (line 391)\n- 30-second timeout with ping keepalive (line 401-407)\n- On disconnect: schedules 10-second grace period before killing persistent agent (line 417)\n- On reconnect: cancels pending disconnect cleanup (line 381)\n\n**Internal pub-sub** (line 22-54):\n- `_session_subscribers` dict maps session_id → list of Queue objects\n- `_broadcast()` pushes events to all subscribers for a session (line 43-54)\n- Background tasks call `_broadcast()` to push tokens/errors to SSE clients (line 280-305, 314-336)\n\n#### 4. Keep-Alive Manager (`services/keepalive_manager.py:1-470`)\n\n**Singleton persistent agent** via tmux + file-based messaging (line 73-74).\n\n**Architecture**:\n- At most one tmux pane active at a time (line 77, 98)\n- Uses `claude-teams` library for inbox messaging (imported at line 21-27)\n- Team directory: `~/.claude/teams/vista-chat-{session_id}` (line 31, 101)\n\n**Lifecycle methods**:\n\n**`start()`** (line 85-139):\n- Kills existing agent if any (line 98-99)\n- Creates team via `teams.create_team()` (line 111)\n- Spawns Claude agent in tmux pane (line 117-126)\n- Stores `_LiveSession` dataclass with session_id, team_name, pane_id (line 133-138)\n\n**`send_message()`** (line 141-160):\n- Validates session matches current agent (line 145-146)\n- Sends plain message via `messaging.send_plain_message()` to \"architect\" agent (line 154-160)\n\n**`poll_response()`** (line 162-199):\n- AsyncGenerator that polls agent inbox every 0.5s (line 174)\n- Reads unread messages via `messaging.read_inbox()` (line 177-182)\n- Yields first message from \"architect\" as token + done event (line 184-189)\n- Timeout after 120s (line 163, 199)\n- Bails early if pane dies (line 195-197)\n\n**`resume()`** (line 207-231):\n- Attempts to reconnect to existing team/pane from previous session\n- Validates pane is still alive via `_is_pane_alive()` (line 219)\n- Restores internal state if successful (line 220-226)\n\n**`stop()`** (line 233-246):\n- Cancels disconnect cleanup task (line 238)\n- Kills tmux pane via `_tmux_kill_pane()` (line 244)\n- Force-deletes team directories (line 245)\n\n**Disconnect grace period** (line 272-292):\n- `schedule_disconnect_cleanup()`: Starts 10-second timer on SSE disconnect (line 272-286)\n- `cancel_disconnect_cleanup()`: Cancels timer on SSE reconnect (line 288-292)\n- Prevents killing agent if user's browser momentarily loses connection\n\n**Tmux spawning** (`_spawn_agent`, line 335-422):\n- Bypasses `spawn_teammate()` due to MSYS2 tmux bug with `#{pane_id}` format strings (line 11, 347)\n- Snapshot pane IDs before spawn, diff after to find new pane (line 388-404)\n- Uses `%N` format (stable unique ID) instead of `session:window.pane` (line 350)\n- Updates team config with actual pane ID (line 407-412)\n\n**Tmux detection** (line 34-56):\n- Searches for tmux in standard MSYS2 paths on Windows (line 35-37)\n- Adds to PATH if found (line 42-51)\n\n#### 5. Diagram Watcher (`services/diagram_watcher.py:1-161`)\n\n**Polling-based file watcher** for `.mmd` and `.drawio` files (line 16).\n\n**Architecture**:\n- Polls every 2 seconds (line 15)\n- Tracks mtime per file in `_file_states` dict (line 22)\n- Single background `_poll_loop` task serves all subscriptions (line 27, 48-49)\n\n**Subscription model** (line 32-65):\n- `subscribe()` returns an asyncio.Queue for the caller (line 32-51)\n- Multiple subscribers per `{project_id}:{feature_name}` key (line 29, 38-45)\n- `unsubscribe()` removes queue and cleans up when no subscribers remain (line 53-65)\n\n**Events** (line 91-114):\n- `diagram_added`: New file detected (line 95-100)\n- `diagram_changed`: mtime changed (line 101-106)\n- `diagram_removed`: File no longer exists (line 109-114)\n- Each event includes file content (line 96, 102) read via `_read_file()` (line 139-144)\n\n**Broadcasting** (line 119-137):\n- `_broadcast()` pushes event dict to all subscriber queues (line 126-137)\n- Dead queues (QueueFull) are automatically removed (line 129-137)\n\n#### 6. Configuration (`config.py:1-300`)\n\n**Directory structure** (line 8-17):\n- `PLUGIN_ROOT`: Plugin install directory (`vista/`)\n- `PORTABLE_DIR`: `vista/portable/` (loop script templates)\n- `DATA_DIR`: `~/.vista/data/` (persistent data, migrated from plugin dir in v1.3.12)\n- `PROJECTS_FILE`: `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- `SETTINGS_FILE`: `~/.vista/settings.json` (configurable via `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` env var)\n\n**Settings structure**:\n- `server`: auto_start, auto_open_browser, host, port (line 38-43)\n- `ralph`: defaults, summarizer, providers, sandbox (line 45-70)\n- `tools.teams`: claude_binary, opencode_url, opencode_auto_start (line 72-80)\n\n**Loading and merging** (line 91-138):\n- `load_settings()`: Reads JSON file, returns `{}` on failure (line 91-99)\n- `_merge_dicts()`: Recursive dict merge (line 123-130)\n- `get_ralph_settings()`: Merges defaults with user overrides (line 133-138)\n- `get_server_settings()`: Env vars override JSON (line 229-252)\n\n**Legacy migration** (line 102-121):\n- One-time migration from `vista/settings.json` to `~/.vista/settings.json` (line 102-120)\n- Non-fatal if migration fails (line 118-120)\n\n**Windows PATH fix** (`ensure_full_path`, line 255-293):\n- Merges system+user PATH from registry on Windows (line 267-288)\n- Fixes stripped PATH in git-bash/IDE contexts (line 257-261)\n- Safe to call multiple times (line 263)\n\n#### 7. Ralph Service (`services/ralph_service.py:1-100+`)\n\n**Job lifecycle manager** for native subprocess and Docker sandbox execution.\n\n**Job creation** (line 40-59):\n- Routes to `_create_native_job()` or `_create_sandboxed_job()` based on `sandbox` flag (line 51-58)\n- Generates UUID job_id (line 72)\n- Job directory: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` (line 73)\n\n**Native job flow** (`_create_native_job`, line 61-100+):\n- Clears runtime artifacts (`output.log`, `loop.ps1`, etc.) at line 76\n- **Plan mode feature dir resolution**: If mode==\"plan\" and feature dir exists, use it as working dir instead of job dir (line 82-83)\n  - This ensures multiple plan loops overwrite the same `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (line 81)\n- Writes `task.md` to feature dir (line 85-86)\n- Generates prompt file from template (line 88-98)\n- Generates loop script from `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` (imported from `portable/ralph.py` at line 16)\n\n**Provider integration** (line 19):\n- Imports `Provider` class from `provider_service.py`\n- Provider's `get_invocation()` method generates shell snippet for loop script\n\n**Output parsing** (line 18):\n- Imports `parse_plaintext_activity` and `parse_stream_json_activity`\n- Parser dispatch logic in ralph routes (routes/ralph.py:88-91)\n\n**Sandbox support** (line 21-29):\n- Lazy-imports Docker-related modules only when `sandbox=True`\n- Modules: `ContainerManager`, `CredentialMounter`, `BashLoopGenerator`\n- Avoids Docker SDK dependency for native jobs\n\n#### 8. Application Entry Point (`app.py:34-334`)\n\n**FastAPI app** created at line 34 with lifespan context manager.\n\n**Router registration** (line 44-70):\n- Imports all route modules (line 44-57)\n- Includes routers via `app.include_router()` (line 59-70)\n\n**Dashboard pages**:\n- `GET /`: Project list dashboard (line 177-203)\n- `GET /project/{project_id}`: Project detail with loop controls (line 206-233)\n- `GET /ralph/jobs`: Ralph jobs list (line 236-254)\n- `GET /ralph/jobs/{job_id}`: Job detail with progress/artifacts (line 257-327)\n- `GET /ralph/settings`: Settings configuration page (line 330-333)\n\n**API endpoints**:\n- `GET /api/health`: Health check with running loop count (line 73-85)\n- `GET /api/loops/running`: Active loops summary for global status bar (line 88-174)\n  - Merges project loops and ralph jobs (line 123-171)\n  - Refreshes ralph job PIDs to avoid stale \"running\" status (line 130-133)\n\n**Loop activity aggregation** (line 88-174):\n- Collects from two sources: `loop_service.get_all_states()` and `ralph_service.list_jobs()`\n- Includes recent actions (last 3) for each loop (line 103, 136-145)\n- Calculates progress percentage from iteration/max_iterations (line 98-100, 147-151)\n- Returns unified list sorted by start_time (line 173-174)\n\n#### 9. MCP Server (`mcp_server.py:1-200`)\n\n**Process model**: MCP server (stdio) wraps FastAPI dashboard as daemon thread (line 1-9).\n\n**Dashboard thread** (`_run_uvicorn_in_thread`, line 92-101):\n- Imports `server.app` at runtime (line 95)\n- Creates `uvicorn.Server` with `log_level=\"warning\"` (line 97)\n- Starts in daemon thread (line 99-100)\n\n**Port allocation** (`_find_free_port`, line 80-89):\n- Incrementally searches for available port starting from preferred (line 82-88)\n\n**OpenCode server launcher** (`_start_opencode_serve`, line 116-144):\n- Spawns `opencode serve --port {port}` subprocess (line 122-127)\n- Polls `/agent` endpoint for up to 10s to confirm readiness (line 130-143)\n\n**Spawn tool description builder** (line 150-200):\n- Dynamically generates tool description based on discovered backends/models\n- Lists available Claude models (line 176) and OpenCode models (line 178-181)\n- Includes OpenCode agent types if server is running (line 184-191)\n\n### Data Flow\n\n#### Chat Session Flow (Persistent Mode)\n\n1. **Session creation** (`POST /api/projects/{pid}/chat/sessions`, chat_sessions.py:93)\n   - Creates ChatSession model (line 99-105)\n   - If mode==\"persistent\": spawns Claude agent via `keepalive_manager.start()` (line 108-128)\n   - Returns session dict with team_name (line 133)\n\n2. **Message send** (`POST /sessions/{sid}/messages`, line 167)\n   - Saves user message (line 192)\n   - Checks if agent is alive via `keepalive_manager.is_alive()` (line 202)\n   - If dead but team_name exists: attempts `keepalive_manager.resume()` (line 205-206)\n   - If still dead: cold starts agent with full history (line 209-228)\n   - If alive: sends just the new message via `keepalive_manager.send_message()` (line 237)\n   - Spawns background task `_stream_response_keepalive()` (line 239-241)\n\n3. **Response streaming** (`_stream_response_keepalive`, line 308)\n   - Polls agent inbox via `keepalive_manager.poll_response()` (line 314)\n   - Broadcasts token events to SSE subscribers (line 315-319)\n   - Saves assistant message when done (line 322)\n   - Broadcasts message_done event (line 323-326)\n\n4. **SSE client connection** (`GET /sessions/{sid}/stream`, line 369)\n   - Subscribes to chat queue (line 384)\n   - Subscribes to diagram watcher queue (line 388)\n   - Merges both queues via forwarder tasks (line 394-395)\n   - Yields events to client (line 401-407)\n   - On disconnect: schedules 10s grace period to kill agent (line 417)\n\n#### Ralph Job Flow (Native)\n\n1. **Job creation** (ralph_service.py:40-59)\n   - Calls `_create_native_job()` (line 56-59)\n   - Generates job dir: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` (line 73)\n   - Writes task.md, prompt, and loop script (line 85-98)\n\n2. **Job execution** (not shown in read sections)\n   - Spawns subprocess running loop script\n   - Script streams output to `output.log`\n   - Script writes progress summaries to `progress.txt`\n\n3. **Status monitoring** (routes/ralph.py:56-65)\n   - `get_job_status()` reads `job.json` + checks PID liveness\n   - Returns status dict with current iteration, progress tail\n\n4. **Progress display** (routes/ralph.py:68-92)\n   - Dashboard always reads `output.log` (line 74)\n   - Dispatches to parser based on provider: `parse_stream_json_activity` for Claude, `parse_plaintext_activity` for others (line 88-91)\n   - Returns last N parsed activity lines (line 92)\n\n### Key Patterns\n\n#### Publisher-Subscriber Pattern\n\n**LoopService** (not fully shown but referenced in app.py:29, 77-79):\n- Broadcasts loop state changes to SSE clients\n- Multiple routes subscribe to loop activity\n\n**DiagramWatcher** (diagram_watcher.py:12-161):\n- Polls file system, broadcasts changes to subscribers\n- Each SSE client gets a dedicated queue (line 44)\n\n**ChatSessionRoutes** (chat_sessions.py:22-54):\n- Internal pub-sub for chat events\n- Background tasks broadcast to all SSE connections for a session\n\n#### Service Layer Pattern\n\nAll business logic encapsulated in `server/services/`:\n- Routes are thin wrappers calling service methods\n- Services manage state and persistence\n- Clear separation: routes handle HTTP, services handle domain logic\n\n#### Provider Strategy Pattern\n\n**Provider base class** (provider_service.py:93-172):\n- Abstract interface for CLI agent providers\n- Implementations: ClaudeProvider, OpenCodeProvider\n- Allows adding new providers without changing core logic\n\n#### File-Based Persistence\n\n**No database**: All data stored as JSON files:\n- Projects: `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n- Sessions: `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`\n- Settings: `~/.vista/settings.json`\n- Job metadata: `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/job.json`\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Settings file**: `~/.vista/settings.json` (config.py:36)\n\n**Environment variable overrides** (config.py:235-250):\n- `RALPH_SERVER_HOST` → server.host\n- `RALPH_SERVER_PORT` → server.port\n- `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_START` → server.auto_start (bool)\n- `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_OPEN` → server.auto_open_browser (bool)\n- `VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE` → custom settings path (line 28-32)\n\n**Ralph defaults** (config.py:46-56):\n- Provider: \"claude\"\n- Model: \"sonnet\"\n- Iterations: 3\n- Summarizer: claude/haiku\n\n**Sandbox defaults** (config.py:58-70):\n- Enabled: false\n- Image: \"vista-ralph:latest\"\n- Network: enabled\n- TTL: 7200 seconds\n- Credential mounts: claude_auth, git_ssh, git_config, gh_cli, opencode (all enabled)\n\n### Error Handling\n\n**Chat service** (chat_service.py):\n- Timeout: Returns error tuple `(False, \"Request timed out\")` (line 161)\n- CLI error: Returns `(False, f\"CLI error (code {rc}): {stderr}\")` (line 167-170)\n- Cancellation: Returns `(False, \"Request was cancelled\")` (line 169)\n\n**Streaming** (chat_service.py:174-301):\n- Yields `{\"type\": \"error\", \"detail\": \"...\"}` on failure (line 188, 274, 297)\n- Catches `asyncio.CancelledError` to call `cancel()` (line 294-295)\n\n**Keep-alive manager** (keepalive_manager.py):\n- Poll timeout: Yields error event after 120s (line 199)\n- Pane death: Yields error event immediately (line 196)\n\n**Ralph service** (ralph_service.py):\n- Raises `ValueError` if prompt template not found (line 95)\n\n### Dependencies\n\n**Key external libraries** (inferred from imports):\n- `fastapi`: Web framework\n- `uvicorn`: ASGI server\n- `sse_starlette`: Server-sent events support (chat_sessions.py:11)\n- `pydantic`: Request/response validation\n- `claude_teams`: Claude agent spawning and messaging (keepalive_manager.py:21-27)\n- `fastmcp`: MCP protocol implementation (mcp_server.py:35-38)\n\n**Docker SDK** (optional, lazy-imported):\n- `docker`: Container management (ralph_service.py:27-29)\n- Only imported when sandbox mode is enabled\n\n### Plugin Manifest\n\n**File**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\.claude-plugin\\plugin.json`\n\n**Current version**: 1.3.15 (line 3)\n\n**Metadata**:\n- Name: \"vista\"\n- Description: \"Visual feature planning with review gate between specs and implementation\"\n- Author: Grove\n- Keywords: planning, visualization, review, feature, jtbd\n\n### Test Structure (`vista/tests/`)\n\n**Unit tests**:\n- `test_output_parser.py`: Parser logic\n- `test_progress_service.py`: Feature scanning\n- `test_project_service.py`: Project CRUD\n- `test_loop_service.py`: Loop lifecycle\n- `test_ralph_service.py`: Ralph job management\n- `test_summarizer_service.py`: AI summarization\n- Sandbox-related: `test_docker_client.py`, `test_container_manager.py`, `test_credential_mounter.py`, `test_bash_loop_generator.py`\n\n**Integration tests** (`tests/integration/`):\n- `test_ralph_lifecycle.py`: End-to-end ralph job flow\n- `test_mcp_tools.py`: MCP tool invocation\n- `test_docker_sandbox.py`: Sandbox execution\n\n**Test fixtures** (`conftest.py`):\n- Provides shared fixtures for projects, sessions, temp directories\n\n### Key Files Referenced\n\nAll absolute paths:\n\n- **Server entry**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\app.py`\n- **MCP wrapper**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\mcp_server.py`\n- **Config**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\config.py`\n- **Chat models**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py`\n- **Chat service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_service.py`\n- **Session service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py`\n- **Keep-alive manager**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\keepalive_manager.py`\n- **Diagram watcher**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\diagram_watcher.py`\n- **Provider service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\provider_service.py`\n- **Ralph service**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py`\n- **Output parser**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\services\\output_parser.py`\n- **Session routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat_sessions.py`\n- **Chat routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat.py`\n- **Ralph routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py`\n- **Architecture routes**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\