{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrsiJaKtb3r4iJ1LJ6zm7v","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Architecture Chat (v2)\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→Replace the subprocess-based CLI chat with two protocol-native provider backends:\n     6→1. **Claude** via Companion fork's WebSocket bridge (`vista/companion/`)\n     7→2. **OpenCode** via `opencode serve` HTTP REST + SSE streaming\n     8→\n     9→Vista's FastAPI server remains the single hub. The existing Jinja2/vanilla JS frontend is kept; Companion's React UI is NOT used. One active chat session at a time, provider locked per session.\n    10→\n    11→### Key Corrections from v1 Plan\n    12→\n    13→- Companion's browser WebSocket message type is `user_message` (not `user`) per `session-types.ts`\n    14→- Companion uses `--permission-mode` flag (not `--dangerously-skip-permissions`)\n    15→- OpenCode streaming uses `prompt_async` + SSE `/event` (not blocking `message`)\n    16→- `mcp_server.py` already has `_start_opencode_serve()` — consolidate, don't duplicate\n    17→- ChatSession model needs `backend_session_id` field for session mapping\n    18→- Windows needs `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` for all subprocess spawning\n    19→\n    20→---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe920b97-a686-4daa-9f39-67e009025eb9","uuid":"f3e281b9-6775-409a-a54a-7abf33467e61","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/architecture-chat/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Architecture Chat (v2)\n\n## Overview\n\nReplace the subprocess-based CLI chat with two protocol-native provider backends:\n1. **Claude** via Companion fork's WebSocket bridge (`vista/companion/`)\n2. **OpenCode** via `opencode serve` HTTP REST + SSE streaming\n\nVista's FastAPI server remains the single hub. The existing Jinja2/vanilla JS frontend is kept; Companion's React UI is NOT used. One active chat session at a time, provider locked per session.\n\n### Key Corrections from v1 Plan\n\n- Companion's browser WebSocket message type is `user_message` (not `user`) per `session-types.ts`\n- Companion uses `--permission-mode` flag (not `--dangerously-skip-permissions`)\n- OpenCode streaming uses `prompt_async` + SSE `/event` (not blocking `message`)\n- `mcp_server.py` already has `_start_opencode_serve()` — consolidate, don't duplicate\n- ChatSession model needs `backend_session_id` field for session mapping\n- Windows needs `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` for all subprocess spawning\n\n---","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1081}}}
