{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nfaq4fWeXj3Jm35kE7UW7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Build the architecture-chat feature following the implementation plan.\n     2→\n     3→## Implementation Plan\n     4→\n     5→The full plan is at: `.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n     6→Also available at: `.vista/features/architecture-chat/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n     7→\n     8→READ THE FULL PLAN BEFORE STARTING. It has 8 phases with detailed code, file locations, and dependencies.\n     9→\n    10→## Reference Documents\n    11→\n    12→- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/domain-requirements.md` — Full requirements\n    13→- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/opencode-server-reference.md` — OpenCode REST API + SSE reference\n    14→- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/companion-websocket-reference.md` — Companion WebSocket protocol reference\n    15→- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/arch/*.mmd` — Architecture diagrams\n    16→\n    17→## Companion Fork\n    18→\n    19→The Companion WebSocket bridge is already cloned at `vista/companion/`. Read its source code for integration:\n    20→- `vista/companion/web/server/index.ts` — Server entry\n    21→- `vista/companion/web/server/cli-launcher.ts` — CLI process management\n    22→- `vista/companion/web/server/routes.ts` — API routes\n    23→- `vista/companion/web/server/ws-bridge.ts` — WebSocket bridge\n    24→- `vista/companion/web/server/session-types.ts` — Protocol types\n    25→\n    26→## Build Order (from plan)\n    27→\n    28→Follow the implementation order in the plan:\n    29→1. Phase 1: `service_lifecycle.py` + `service_status.py` route + `app.py` lifespan\n    30→2. Phase 3: `diagram_watcher.py` rewrite (polling → watchdog)\n    31→3. Phase 4: `context_assembler.py` extraction\n    32→4. Phase 2: `claude_ws_client.py`, `opencode_client.py`, `provider_router.py`, then `chat_service.py` + `chat_sessions.py` rewrite\n    33→5. Phase 5: `provider_service.py` model discovery\n    34→6. Phase 6: `architecture.html` frontend changes\n    35→7. Phase 7: Companion fork verification\n    36→8. Phase 8: Final integration + `mcp_server.py` cleanup\n    37→\n    38→## Key Constraints\n    39→\n    40→- All code goes in `vista/server/` (Python) — NOT in the companion directory\n    41→- Windows-first: use CREATE_NO_WINDOW, taskkill /T /F /PID\n    42→- New Python deps: watchdog, websockets, httpx\n    43→- Keep existing tests passing\n    44→- Run tests with: `python -m pytest tests/ -q` (from vista/ dir)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41eb5763-1813-40b4-994f-a8833bfca10e","uuid":"20ba087e-e88d-482a-8f15-04ea45506f0f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/arch-chat-build-5d505475/task.md","content":"Build the architecture-chat feature following the implementation plan.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\nThe full plan is at: `.vista/ralph/architecture-chat-plan-86118b3b/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\nAlso available at: `.vista/features/architecture-chat/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`\n\nREAD THE FULL PLAN BEFORE STARTING. It has 8 phases with detailed code, file locations, and dependencies.\n\n## Reference Documents\n\n- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/domain-requirements.md` — Full requirements\n- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/opencode-server-reference.md` — OpenCode REST API + SSE reference\n- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/specs/companion-websocket-reference.md` — Companion WebSocket protocol reference\n- `.vista/features/architecture-chat/arch/*.mmd` — Architecture diagrams\n\n## Companion Fork\n\nThe Companion WebSocket bridge is already cloned at `vista/companion/`. Read its source code for integration:\n- `vista/companion/web/server/index.ts` — Server entry\n- `vista/companion/web/server/cli-launcher.ts` — CLI process management\n- `vista/companion/web/server/routes.ts` — API routes\n- `vista/companion/web/server/ws-bridge.ts` — WebSocket bridge\n- `vista/companion/web/server/session-types.ts` — Protocol types\n\n## Build Order (from plan)\n\nFollow the implementation order in the plan:\n1. Phase 1: `service_lifecycle.py` + `service_status.py` route + `app.py` lifespan\n2. Phase 3: `diagram_watcher.py` rewrite (polling → watchdog)\n3. Phase 4: `context_assembler.py` extraction\n4. Phase 2: `claude_ws_client.py`, `opencode_client.py`, `provider_router.py`, then `chat_service.py` + `chat_sessions.py` rewrite\n5. Phase 5: `provider_service.py` model discovery\n6. Phase 6: `architecture.html` frontend changes\n7. Phase 7: Companion fork verification\n8. Phase 8: Final integration + `mcp_server.py` cleanup\n\n## Key Constraints\n\n- All code goes in `vista/server/` (Python) — NOT in the companion directory\n- Windows-first: use CREATE_NO_WINDOW, taskkill /T /F /PID\n- New Python deps: watchdog, websockets, httpx\n- Keep existing tests passing\n- Run tests with: `python -m pytest tests/ -q` (from vista/ dir)","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
