{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtRnQgzX5TLNJccgX4QBJR","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 7958c52f7eccd3ab207bcbcf73b675b27ff31b16\nAuthor: ribeec20 <ribeec2002@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Feb 12 15:48:48 2026 -0800\n\n    feat(arch-chat): Add protocol-native provider backends for architecture chat\n    \n    Replace subprocess-based CLI chat with two protocol-native provider backends:\n    - Claude via Companion WebSocket bridge (claude_ws_client.py)\n    - OpenCode via REST API + SSE streaming (opencode_client.py)\n    \n    New components:\n    - ServiceLifecycleManager: Auto-start/stop/restart Companion and OpenCode\n      as managed services with health checks and exponential backoff\n    - ProviderRouter: Routes chat messages to correct backend, manages\n      session mapping between Vista and backend session IDs\n    - ContextAssembler: Clean, testable prompt assembly extracted from ChatService\n    - Service status API + frontend health indicators\n    \n    Key changes:\n    - chat_sessions.py: Three streaming paths (ProviderRouter protocol-native,\n      keepalive_manager persistent/tmux, CLI fallback)\n    - ChatSession model: Added backend_session_id field\n    - provider_service.py: Live model discovery from running OpenCode server\n    - architecture.html: Service status dots + health polling every 10s\n    - app.py: Lifecycle manager integration in lifespan\n    \n    342 unit tests passing (28 new), 0 failures. Bump to v1.4.0.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .../architecture-chat/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md       | 1059 +++++++++++++------\n .../IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                         | 1101 ++++++++++++++++++++\n .vista/ralph/arch-chat-build-5d505475/progress.txt |   46 +\n vista/.claude-plugin/plugin.json                   |    2 +-\n vista/server/app.py                                |   18 +\n vista/server/config.py                             |   14 +\n vista/se