{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BfBQ69z6xYBHXvSghdMnkh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→Iteration: 1\n     3→Time: 2026-02-12\n     4→\n     5→WHAT WAS DONE:\n     6→\n     7→Phase 1 - Service Lifecycle Manager:\n     8→- server/services/service_lifecycle.py: NEW - Full lifecycle manager with state machine (Stopped->Starting->Running->Stopping->Error->Restarting), periodic health checks, exponential backoff restarts, Windows process tree kill, bun binary discovery, companion_config() and opencode_config() factory functions\n     9→- server/routes/service_status.py: NEW - GET /api/services/health endpoint returning all managed service statuses\n    10→\n    11→Phase 2 - Provider Router (Claude WS + OpenCode SSE):\n    12→- server/services/claude_ws_client.py: NEW - WebSocket client for Companion's browser-side WS bridge. Handles session create/connect/send_message/disconnect/delete_session. Protocol-correct: user_message, stream_event, permission_response with behavior:\"allow\", result with data wrapper\n    13→- server/services/opencode_client.py: NEW - HTTP+SSE client for OpenCode REST API. Handles session CRUD, prompt_async + SSE event streaming, Basic Auth from env var\n    14→- server/services/provider_router.py: NEW - Routes messages to correct backend based on provider type. Manages session mapping (Vista session_id -> backend session_id). Singleton instance\n    15→\n    16→Phase 4 - Context Assembler:\n    17→- server/services/context_assembler.py: NEW - Extracted prompt assembly from ChatService into clean, testable module. build_system_prompt(), build_full_prompt(), get_diagram_context() static methods\n    18→\n    19→Phase 5 - Model Discovery:\n    20→- server/services/provider_service.py: MODIFIED - OpenCodeProvider.get_models() now tries running OpenCode server HTTP API first (GET /config/providers), falls back to CLI. Extracted _get_models_from_cli() helper\n    21→\n    22→Phase 6 - Frontend:\n    23→- server/views/architecture.html: MODIFIED - Added service status indicator bar with green/red dots for Companion and OpenCode. Added pollServiceHealth() JS function polling /api/services/health every 10s. Added updateProviderAvailability() to show \"(offline)\" on unavailable providers\n    24→\n    25→Phase 8 - Integration:\n    26→- server/app.py: MODIFIED - Import lifecycle manager + provider_router. Lifespan now registers companion/opencode configs, calls start_all() on startup, cleanup_all()+stop_all() on shutdown. Added service_status router\n    27→- server/config.py: MODIFIED - Added get_chat_settings() with companion_port/opencode_port defaults\n    28→- server/models/chat_session.py: MODIFIED - Added backend_session_id field to ChatSession, updated to_dict(), to_summary_dict(), from_dict()\n    29→- server/routes/chat_sessions.py: REWRITTEN - Uses ContextAssembler for prompt building. Three streaming paths: (1) ProviderRouter for protocol-native when backend available, (2) keepalive_manager for persistent/tmux mode, (3) CLI fallback via ChatService. Backend session creation on first message. Cleanup backend on session delete\n    30→- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: Bumped version to 1.4.0\n    31→\n    32→Tests:\n    33→- tests/test_context_assembler.py: NEW - 11 tests for prompt assembly, diagram context reading, system prompt\n    34→- tests/test_service_lifecycle.py: NEW - 12 tests for state machine, config, registration, prerequisite checking, port finding\n    35→- tests/test_provider_router.py: NEW - 5 tests for initial state, cleanup, unknown provider handling\n    36→- Total: 342 unit tests passing (28 new + 314 existing), 0 failures\n    37→\n    38→WHAT WAS NOT DONE:\n    39→\n    40→- Phase 3 (diagram_watcher.py rewrite to watchdog): DEFERRED - The existing polling watcher works correctly. Watchdog upgrade is an optimization, not a functional requirement. Can be done in a follow-up iteration\n    41→- Phase 7 (Companion fork verification): DONE IMPLICITLY - No changes needed to companion/ as confirmed by plan. Bun discovery logic is in service_lifecycle.py\n    42→- keepalive_manager.py removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with persistent/tmux mode. The new ProviderRouter is the primary path; keepalive_manager is a secondary fallback\n    43→- chat.py route removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with any clients using the legacy blocking endpoint\n    44→\n    45→Tests: 342 passing, 0 failing (unit tests only; integration tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this change)\n    46→---\n    47→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41eb5763-1813-40b4-994f-a8833bfca10e","uuid":"de7da292-049e-4880-929c-76b9b27909e9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista\\.vista\\ralph\\arch-chat-build-5d505475\\progress.txt","content":"---\nIteration: 1\nTime: 2026-02-12\n\nWHAT WAS DONE:\n\nPhase 1 - Service Lifecycle Manager:\n- server/services/service_lifecycle.py: NEW - Full lifecycle manager with state machine (Stopped->Starting->Running->Stopping->Error->Restarting), periodic health checks, exponential backoff restarts, Windows process tree kill, bun binary discovery, companion_config() and opencode_config() factory functions\n- server/routes/service_status.py: NEW - GET /api/services/health endpoint returning all managed service statuses\n\nPhase 2 - Provider Router (Claude WS + OpenCode SSE):\n- server/services/claude_ws_client.py: NEW - WebSocket client for Companion's browser-side WS bridge. Handles session create/connect/send_message/disconnect/delete_session. Protocol-correct: user_message, stream_event, permission_response with behavior:\"allow\", result with data wrapper\n- server/services/opencode_client.py: NEW - HTTP+SSE client for OpenCode REST API. Handles session CRUD, prompt_async + SSE event streaming, Basic Auth from env var\n- server/services/provider_router.py: NEW - Routes messages to correct backend based on provider type. Manages session mapping (Vista session_id -> backend session_id). Singleton instance\n\nPhase 4 - Context Assembler:\n- server/services/context_assembler.py: NEW - Extracted prompt assembly from ChatService into clean, testable module. build_system_prompt(), build_full_prompt(), get_diagram_context() static methods\n\nPhase 5 - Model Discovery:\n- server/services/provider_service.py: MODIFIED - OpenCodeProvider.get_models() now tries running OpenCode server HTTP API first (GET /config/providers), falls back to CLI. Extracted _get_models_from_cli() helper\n\nPhase 6 - Frontend:\n- server/views/architecture.html: MODIFIED - Added service status indicator bar with green/red dots for Companion and OpenCode. Added pollServiceHealth() JS function polling /api/services/health every 10s. Added updateProviderAvailability() to show \"(offline)\" on unavailable providers\n\nPhase 8 - Integration:\n- server/app.py: MODIFIED - Import lifecycle manager + provider_router. Lifespan now registers companion/opencode configs, calls start_all() on startup, cleanup_all()+stop_all() on shutdown. Added service_status router\n- server/config.py: MODIFIED - Added get_chat_settings() with companion_port/opencode_port defaults\n- server/models/chat_session.py: MODIFIED - Added backend_session_id field to ChatSession, updated to_dict(), to_summary_dict(), from_dict()\n- server/routes/chat_sessions.py: REWRITTEN - Uses ContextAssembler for prompt building. Three streaming paths: (1) ProviderRouter for protocol-native when backend available, (2) keepalive_manager for persistent/tmux mode, (3) CLI fallback via ChatService. Backend session creation on first message. Cleanup backend on session delete\n- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: Bumped version to 1.4.0\n\nTests:\n- tests/test_context_assembler.py: NEW - 11 tests for prompt assembly, diagram context reading, system prompt\n- tests/test_service_lifecycle.py: NEW - 12 tests for state machine, config, registration, prerequisite checking, port finding\n- tests/test_provider_router.py: NEW - 5 tests for initial state, cleanup, unknown provider handling\n- Total: 342 unit tests passing (28 new + 314 existing), 0 failures\n\nWHAT WAS NOT DONE:\n\n- Phase 3 (diagram_watcher.py rewrite to watchdog): DEFERRED - The existing polling watcher works correctly. Watchdog upgrade is an optimization, not a functional requirement. Can be done in a follow-up iteration\n- Phase 7 (Companion fork verification): DONE IMPLICITLY - No changes needed to companion/ as confirmed by plan. Bun discovery logic is in service_lifecycle.py\n- keepalive_manager.py removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with persistent/tmux mode. The new ProviderRouter is the primary path; keepalive_manager is a secondary fallback\n- chat.py route removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with any clients using the legacy blocking endpoint\n\nTests: 342 passing, 0 failing (unit tests only; integration tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this change)\n---\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}}}
