code URL. Updated lifespan to remove opencode_process variable and cleanup code. No more duplicate process spawning\n\nLegacy Code Removal:\n- server/services/keepalive_manager.py: DELETED (git rm) - tmux-based persistent chat manager fully replaced by ProviderRouter WebSocket/SSE\n- server/routes/chat.py: DELETED (git rm) - Legacy blocking POST /api/projects/{id}/chat endpoint superseded by streaming sessions\n- server/routes/chat_sessions.py: REWRITTEN - Removed all keepalive_manager imports and usage. Removed persistent mode code path entirely. Removed mode field from CreateSessionRequest and SendMessageRequest. Removed _stream_response_keepalive() function. Simplified delete_session, cancel_session_chat, and stream_session endpoints\n- server/app.py: MODIFIED - Removed keepalive_manager import and shutdown call. Removed chat router import and inclusion. Removed chat_service import. Bumped version to 1.4.1\n- tests/test_architecture.py: MODIFIED - Removed TestChatAPI class (7 tests for deleted chat.py endpoint)\n- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: Bumped version to 1.4.1\n\nWHAT WAS NOT DONE:\n\n- All deferred items from Iteration 1 are now DONE (Phase 3, mcp_server.py cleanup, keepalive/chat removal)\n- No remaining deferred items\n\nTests: 362 unit tests passing, 0 failures, 3 warnings (pre-existing coroutine warnings)\n---","originalFile":"---\nIteration: 1\nTime: 2026-02-12\n\nWHAT WAS DONE:\n\nPhase 1 - Service Lifecycle Manager:\n- server/services/service_lifecycle.py: NEW - Full lifecycle manager with state machine (Stopped->Starting->Running->Stopping->Error->Restarting), periodic health checks, exponential backoff restarts, Windows process tree kill, bun binary discovery, companion_config() and opencode_config() factory functions\n- server/routes/service_status.py: NEW - GET /api/services/health endpoint returning all managed service statuses\n\nPhase 2 - Provider Router (Claude WS + OpenCode SSE):\n- server/services/claude_ws_client.py: NEW - WebSocket client for Companion's browser-side WS bridge. Handles session create/connect/send_message/disconnect/delete_session. Protocol-correct: user_message, stream_event, permission_response with behavior:\"allow\", result with data wrapper\n- server/services/opencode_client.py: NEW - HTTP+SSE client for OpenCode REST API. Handles session CRUD, prompt_async + SSE event streaming, Basic Auth from env var\n- server/services/provider_router.py: NEW - Routes messages to correct backend based on provider type. Manages session mapping (Vista session_id -> backend session_id). Singleton instance\n\nPhase 4 - Context Assembler:\n- server/services/context_assembler.py: NEW - Extracted prompt assembly from ChatService into clean, testable module. build_system_prompt(), build_full_prompt(), get_diagram_context() static methods\n\nPhase 5 - Model Discovery:\n- server/services/provider_service.py: MODIFIED - OpenCodeProvider.get_models() now tries running OpenCode server HTTP API first (GET /config/providers), falls back to CLI. Extracted _get_models_from_cli() helper\n\nPhase 6 - Frontend:\n- server/views/architecture.html: MODIFIED - Added service status indicator bar with green/red dots for Companion and OpenCode. Added pollServiceHealth() JS function polling /api/services/health every 10s. Added updateProviderAvailability() to show \"(offline)\" on unavailable providers\n\nPhase 8 - Integration:\n- server/app.py: MODIFIED - Import lifecycle manager + provider_router. Lifespan now registers companion/opencode configs, calls start_all() on startup, cleanup_all()+stop_all() on shutdown. Added service_status router\n- server/config.py: MODIFIED - Added get_chat_settings() with companion_port/opencode_port defaults\n- server/models/chat_session.py: MODIFIED - Added backend_session_id field to ChatSession, updated to_dict(), to_summary_dict(), from_dict()\n- server/routes/chat_sessions.py: REWRITTEN - Uses ContextAssembler for prompt building. Three streaming paths: (1) ProviderRouter for protocol-native when backend available, (2) keepalive_manager for persistent/tmux mode, (3) CLI fallback via ChatService. Backend session creation on first message. Cleanup backend on session delete\n- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: Bumped version to 1.4.0\n\nTests:\n- tests/test_context_assembler.py: NEW - 11 tests for prompt assembly, diagram context reading, system prompt\n- tests/test_service_lifecycle.py: NEW - 12 tests for state machine, config, registration, prerequisite checking, port finding\n- tests/test_provider_router.py: NEW - 5 tests for initial state, cleanup, unknown provider handling\n- Total: 342 unit tests passing (28 new + 314 existing), 0 failures\n\nWHAT WAS NOT DONE:\n\n- Phase 3 (diagram_watcher.py rewrite to watchdog): DEFERRED - The existing polling watcher works correctly. Watchdog upgrade is an optimization, not a functional requirement. Can be done in a follow-up iteration\n- Phase 7 (Companion fork verification): DONE IMPLICITLY - No changes needed to companion/ as confirmed by plan. Bun discovery logic is in service_lifecycle.py\n- keepalive_manager.py removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with persistent/tmux mode. The new ProviderRouter is the primary path; keepalive_manager is a secondary fallback\n- chat.py route removal: DEFERRED - Kept for backward compatibility with any clients using the legacy blocking endpoint\n\nTests: 342 passing, 0 failing (unit tests only; integration tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this change)\n---\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":44,"oldLines":3,"newStart":44,"newLines":32,"lines":[" "," Tests: 342 passing, 0 failing (unit tests only; integration tests have pre-existing failures unrelated to this change)"," ---","+","+---","+Iteration: 2","+Time: 2026-02-12","+","+WHAT WAS DONE:","+","+Phase 3 - Diagram Watcher Rewrite (polling -> watchdog):","+- server/services/diagram_watcher.py: REWRITTEN - Replaced 2s polling loop with watchdog Observer pattern using native Windows ReadDirectoryChangesW. Added _DiagramEventHandler (FileSystemEventHandler subclass) with 100ms debounce via threading.Timer. Thread-safe cross-thread async scheduling via loop.call_soon_threadsafe(). Added _detect_diagram_type() helper for Mermaid diagram classification. Added _update_manifest_sync() for auto-regenerating _arch.json on file add/remove. Same public API preserved: subscribe(), unsubscribe(), stop()","+- tests/test_diagram_watcher.py: NEW - 26 tests covering diagram type detection (8), file reading (2), watcher subscribe/unsubscribe/observer lifecycle (7), manifest auto-update (4), async broadcast (3), stop_all (1)","+","+Phase 8 - mcp_server.py Cleanup:","+- mcp_server.py: MODIFIED - Removed _start_opencode_serve() function that spawned a duplicate opencode process. Replaced with _get_lifecycle_opencode_url() that queries the service_lifecycle singleton for the already-running opencode URL. Updated lifespan to remove opencode_process variable and cleanup code. No more duplicate process spawning","+","+Legacy Code Removal:","+- server/services/keepalive_manager.py: DELETED (git rm) - tmux-based persistent chat manager fully replaced by ProviderRouter WebSocket/SSE","+- server/routes/chat.py: DELETED (git rm) - Legacy blocking POST /api/projects/{id}/chat endpoint superseded by streaming sessions","+- server/routes/chat_sessions.py: REWRITTEN - Removed all keepalive_manager imports and usage. Removed persistent mode code path entirely. Removed mode field from CreateSessionRequest and SendMessageRequest. Removed _stream_response_keepalive() function. Simplified delete_session, cancel_session_chat, and stream_session endpoints","+- server/app.py: MODIFIED - Removed keepalive_manager import and shutdown call. Removed chat router import and inclusion. Removed chat_service import. Bumped version to 1.4.1","+- tests/test_architecture.py: MODIFIED - Removed TestChatAPI class (7 tests for deleted chat.py endpoint)","+- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: Bumped version to 1.4.1","+","+WHAT WAS NOT DONE:","+","+- All deferred items from Iteration 1 are now DONE (Phase 3, mcp_server.py cleanup, keepalive/chat removal)","+- No remaining deferred items","+","+Tests: 362 unit tests passing, 0 failures, 3 warnings (pre-existing coroutine warnings)","+---"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
